  <data name="Corr_WifiInstability_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Possible Wi-Fi Instability</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_WifiInstability_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Poor RF signal conditions appear to be degrading local network performance. RSSI is below acceptable levels, combined with elevated jitter and/or packet loss, while the internet path remains relatively stable.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_WifiInstability_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Move closer to the access point, reduce physical obstructions, or improve AP placement. Verify the client is not connecting to a distant BSSID.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Corr_ExternalNetworkIssue_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Possible External Network Issue</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_ExternalNetworkIssue_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The local network and Wi-Fi connection appear stable, while the external internet path shows elevated latency or probe timeouts. The issue is likely upstream of this device (ISP or WAN).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_ExternalNetworkIssue_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check ISP status, router WAN port, and modem logs. Contact the ISP if the problem persists.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Corr_NetworkInstability_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>General Network Instability</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_NetworkInstability_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Simultaneous degradation detected across both local and internet-side metrics. Both LAN latency and internet latency are elevated, along with jitter and packet loss, indicating a systemic problem.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_NetworkInstability_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check router load, WAN connection health, and local network congestion. Review all active connections and running background services.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Corr_SignalDegradation_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Progressive Signal Decline</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_SignalDegradation_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>RSSI is showing a consistent downward trend over the observation window. This indicates the signal is actively worsening, not just a static low-signal condition.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_SignalDegradation_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The device may be moving away from the AP, or the AP may be reducing power. Monitor the trend and consider repositioning or enabling band steering.</value>
  </data>

  <data name="Corr_PossibleCongestion_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Possible Network Congestion</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_PossibleCongestion_Desc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Elevated and variable latency on both LAN and internet paths, combined with high jitter, suggests possible traffic congestion or bandwidth saturation.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Corr_PossibleCongestion_Rec" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Review active connections and traffic utilization. Check for background downloads, video streaming, or other bandwidth-intensive tasks. Consider QoS configuration.</value>
  </data>
